   "d": 2,
   "title": {
    "ar": "docker compose: API وn8n وPostgres",
    "en": "docker compose: the API, n8n and Postgres"
   },
   "goal": {
    "ar": "تشغّل أكتر من خدمة مع بعض بملف compose واحد: الـ API بتاعك وn8n وPostgres، بشبكة مشتركة وvolumes وhealthchecks وrestart، والأسرار من .env.",
    "en": "Run several services together from one compose file: your API, n8n and Postgres, with a shared network, volumes, healthchecks and restart policies, and secrets from .env."
   },
   "learn": [
    {
     "h": {
      "ar": "ملف compose",
      "en": "A compose file"
     },
     "p": {
      "ar": "`compose.yaml` بيوصف كل الخدمات: الـ image أو build، والبورتات، ومتغيرات البيئة، والـ volumes. `docker compose up -d` بيشغّلهم كلهم، و`docker compose logs -f api` لوج خدمة، و`down` يوقّفهم. الخدمات بتشوف بعض بأساميها: n8n بينادي الـ API على `http://api:8000` (مش localhost).",
      "en": "`compose.yaml` describes every service: the image or build, ports, environment variables and volumes. `docker compose up -d` starts them all, `docker compose logs -f api` shows one service’s log, and `down` stops them. Services reach each other by name: n8n calls the API at `http://api:8000` (not localhost)."
     },
     "ex": "# compose.yaml\nservices:\n  api:\n    build: .\n    env_file: .env\n    volumes: [\"api-data:/app/data\"]\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD\", \"python\", \"-c\", \"import urllib.request; urllib.request.urlopen('http://localhost:8000/health')\"]\n      interval: 30s\n\n  postgres:\n    image: postgres:16\n    environment:\n      POSTGRES_USER: n8n\n      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}\n      POSTGRES_DB: n8n\n    volumes: [\"pg-data:/var/lib/postgresql/data\"]\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    healthcheck:\n      test: [\"CMD-SHELL\", \"pg_isready -U n8n\"]\n      interval: 10s\n\n  n8n:\n    image: docker.n8n.io/n8nio/n8n\n    ports: [\"5678:5678\"]\n    environment:\n      DB_TYPE: postgresdb\n      DB_POSTGRESDB_HOST: postgres\n      DB_POSTGRESDB_USER: n8n\n      DB_POSTGRESDB_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}\n      GENERIC_TIMEZONE: Africa/Cairo\n      N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY: ${N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY}\n    volumes: [\"n8n-data:/home/node/.n8n\"]\n    depends_on:\n      postgres: { condition: service_healthy }\n    restart: unless-stopped\n\nvolumes: { api-data: {}, pg-data: {}, n8n-data: {} }",
     "lang": "text"
    },
    {
     "h": {
      "ar": "الشبكة والأسرار",
      "en": "The network and secrets"
     },
     "p": {
      "ar": "compose بيعمل شبكة داخلية: Postgres مش محتاج بورت مفتوح للعالم — n8n بيوصله جوه الشبكة. افتح للعالم اللي لازم بس (n8n، أو الـ API ورا reverse proxy). القيم زي `${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}` بتيجي من ملف `.env` جنب compose.yaml (اللي مبيترفعش على Git)، و`N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY` احفظه في مكان آمن: من غيره credentials n8n متتفكش لو نقلت السيرفر.",
      "en": "compose creates an internal network: Postgres needs no port open to the world — n8n reaches it inside the network. Expose only what must be public (n8n, or the API behind a reverse proxy). Values like `${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}` come from a `.env` file next to compose.yaml (never committed), and keep `N8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY` somewhere safe: without it n8n’s credentials cannot be decrypted if you move servers."
     },
     "ex": "# .env  (next to compose.yaml, never committed)\nPOSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me-long-random\nN8N_ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-long-random-and-back-it-up\nTOOLS_API_KEY=change-me\n\n# generate random values:\npython -c \"import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))\"\n\n# useful commands\ndocker compose up -d\ndocker compose ps\ndocker compose logs -f n8n\ndocker compose exec postgres psql -U n8n -c \"\\dt\"\ndocker compose pull && docker compose up -d      # update images",
     "lang": "text"
    },
    {
     "h": {
      "ar": "النسخ الاحتياطي",
      "en": "Backups"
     },
     "p": {
      "ar": "الـ volumes هي بياناتك: اعمل نسخة احتياطية منها بانتظام وجرّب ترجّعها (نسخة متجرّبتش = مفيش نسخة). لـ Postgres: `pg_dump` لملف بالتاريخ، واحتفظ بآخر 14 مثلًا، وانقل نسخة لمكان تاني (S3 أو Drive). وصدّر workflows n8n وcredentials (مشفرة) بالـ CLI. سكربت أسبوع 9 + جدولة أسبوع 20 = نسخ احتياطي أوتوماتيك.",
      "en": "Volumes are your data: back them up regularly and test restoring (an untested backup is no backup). For Postgres: `pg_dump` to a dated file, keep the last 14, say, and copy one off the server (S3 or Drive). Export n8n workflows and (encrypted) credentials with its CLI. The week 9 script + week 20 scheduling = automatic backups."
     },
     "ex": "#!/bin/sh\n# backup.sh — run daily by cron\nset -e\nSTAMP=$(date +%Y-%m-%d_%H%M)\nmkdir -p /srv/backups\ndocker compose exec -T postgres pg_dump -U n8n n8n | gzip > /srv/backups/n8n_$STAMP.sql.gz\ndocker compose exec -T n8n n8n export:workflow --all --output=/home/node/.n8n/backup_workflows.json\nls -1t /srv/backups/n8n_*.sql.gz | tail -n +15 | xargs -r rm\n\n# restore test (on another machine):\n# gunzip -c n8n_2026-10-01_0200.sql.gz | docker compose exec -T postgres psql -U n8n n8n",
     "lang": "text"
    }
   ],
